Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Level 2 Certification Project", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9796528989548874`*^9, 
  3.979652906298498*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ecde2c98-1c4f-434f-ae7f-\
9c56a0f53236"],

Cell["\<\
Benjamin Ciotti, benjaminciotti@boisestate.edu
February 12, 2026\
\>", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979652910509388*^9, 3.979652936556101*^9}, {
  3.979653817788103*^9, 3.979653826410877*^9}, {3.979945748207361*^9, 
  3.9799457609276695`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"99eed81e-95cd-7943-b4f0-\
747dcbb2f642"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The goal here is to to use neural networks to predict NFL outcomes.  There \
are many types of outcomes that one can try to predict such as which team \
will win, how much they will win by, whether they will cover the spread (i.e. \
win by more than anticipated), what the (combined) total number of points \
scored will be, and (in my case) ",
 StyleBox["whether the combined total number of points will be less than \
anticipated",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  In the terminology of sports betting I am attempting to predict whether \
the under will hit.\n\nThere is a clear application of such prediction \
models, namely profitable sports betting.  Moreover these techniques may be \
modified to predict outcomes in other sports (which may be of particular \
relevance in the NFL off-season). "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97965331672637*^9, 3.9796535720684376`*^9}, {
   3.9796536177688484`*^9, 3.9796536581070194`*^9}, {3.9796536909489594`*^9, 
   3.9796537774795322`*^9}, {3.9796538531035614`*^9, 
   3.9796538560515137`*^9}, {3.9796538989193554`*^9, 
   3.9796539492107506`*^9}, {3.979813570298195*^9, 3.9798135741383896`*^9}, {
   3.9798142523102894`*^9, 3.97981427701861*^9}, 3.979814336853428*^9, {
   3.979814414160204*^9, 3.9798144230429955`*^9}, {3.979945764191126*^9, 
   3.9799459363533897`*^9}, {3.979945975823412*^9, 3.9799460045940247`*^9}, 
   3.979946070646822*^9},ExpressionUUID->"f5bceb57-973e-3e45-aa0a-\
b81415a7109b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Data Preprocessing", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9798144279280777`*^9, 3.9798144660140114`*^9}, 
   3.9798145611977615`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"eac0dace-e9eb-7d41-92c2-\
abada911192a"],

Cell["\<\
My dataset on NFL game outcomes, nfl_full.csv, was found on Kaggle at \
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/tobycrabtree/nfl-scores-and-betting-data.  It \
contains data on 14358 NFL games going back to the 1960s, and the data \
included point totals, spreads, dates, years, which week of the season a game \
was in, where it was played, what the weather conditions were, whether it was \
a playoff game, who the home team was, who the favorite was, and (crucially) \
spreads (how many points the favorite is expected to win by), over/unders \
(the anticipated total number of points), and how many points each team \
in-fact scored.  

nfl_teams.csv is a supplemental spreadsheet of team names and their \
associated abbreviations and is from the same Kaggle page.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9798144351216793`*^9, {3.9798144815831795`*^9, 3.9798145525977707`*^9}, {
   3.979826462672846*^9, 
   3.979826464286419*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cf158f2d-a891-664e-a7db-\
5c5155274813"],

