Cell[TextData[{
 "We see we still have 10,545 rows of game data so there is still plenty to \
train on.  There would have been far fewer complete rows had I not first \
dropped those last two columns that were missing a lot of entries. \n\nI want \
to replace all the team names with their three-letter abbreviations (or \
team_id) for consistency, since my dataset uses the abbreviations to label \
favorites.  \n\n",
 StyleBox["Note",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": I\[CloseCurlyQuote]m not 100% sure this is a good idea (and a longer \
project would compare my results to those obtained by skipping this step).  \
The issue is that teams occasionally change names or cities, and in my \
analysis I will be treating them as the same team when that happens.  So for \
example the LA Rams and the St. Louis Rams will both be assigned the \
abbreviation LAR.  The Las Vegas Raiders and the Los Angeles Raiders and the \
Oakland Raiders are all assigned LVR.  The Houston Oilers, Tennessee Oilers, \
and Tennessee Titans are all assigned TEN.   \n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979654479312023*^9, 3.979654552009289*^9}, {
  3.9796546150728855`*^9, 3.979654814239767*^9}, {3.9796548463424873`*^9, 
  3.9796548718330383`*^9}, {3.979654943646412*^9, 3.979655109916916*^9}, {
  3.979895108672182*^9, 
  3.97989514981135*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"864dd40c-f27f-8f44-836f-\
e8175a72e9dc"],

