Cell[TextData[{
 "So the raw win rate for unders is about 49.5%, but if we condition upon the \
bet not resulting in a push (wherein the bookie returns your money to you so \
there was effectively no bet) we can compute the ",
 "actual win rate",
 " for unders ",
 "as ",
 StyleBox["underHitProbability/(overHitProbability+underHitProbability)\
\[TildeTilde]50.4%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ".  Similarly the ",
 "actual win rate",
 " for overs is ",
 StyleBox["overHitProbability/(overHitProbability+underHitProbability)\
\[TildeTilde]49.6%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ".  \n\nWe see that unders are more likely to hit than overs so it makes \
more sense to bet on unders than overs.  (",
 StyleBox["Fun fact",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": I had originally written this assignment to predict when to bet on overs \
but rewrote it to bet on unders in light of this fact.)\n\nIt can be shown \
that if an outcome happens with a probability P>50%, then an optimal \
no-additional-information betting strategy is to bet on its occurrence 100% \
of the time (and if P<50% then bet ",
 StyleBox["against",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " it 100% of the time).  So knowing only that the actual win rates for \
unders is 50.4%, we could simply bet on the under 100% of the time and win \
50.4% of decided (non-push) games. If we include pushes this means we want \
bets on the under to win more than 50.4/(50.4+ 49.6+1.85)\[TildeTilde]49.6% \
of the time (i.e. we want to beat the underHitProbability).\n\nBut wait - if \
we are betting in the real world then we have to take the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]vig\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] into account.  Real-world \
bookies don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t offer 50:50 odds on over/unders.  Rather they \
typically offer bets at \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]-110,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
meaning you have to risk $110 to win $100.  It can be shown that, in the \
absence of pushes, this means you have to win over 110/210\[TildeTilde]52.4% \
of such bets in order to be profitable.  If we assume that 1.85% of bets on \
the over/under are pushes then this falls to 110*(1-.0185)/210\[TildeTilde]",
 StyleBox["51.4%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ".  So ",
 StyleBox["this will be my target accuracy rate",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ".  Basically I want my predictions to be correct more than 51.4% of the \
time (or equivalently my error rate to be less than 48.6%)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQBmIQbfFyis+jZW8dv5yZFQ6iM7bZZIHomB8LwfSZ3qvN
