Cell["\<\
In this randomization my accuracy is an impressive 54%, well above the target \
of 51.4%.  That said, not all randomizations of train and test data may yield \
models that perform as well.

In a future project I would write a loop that resamples and retrains so as to \
get a better accuracy estimate (and see the supplemental section for an \
implementation of something like this) and moreover program the loops to \
optimize over different hyperparameter values. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9798336435982265`*^9, 3.9798336491673737`*^9}, {
  3.9799074415350494`*^9, 3.97990751260647*^9}, {3.979907873724531*^9, 
  3.9799078738087673`*^9}, {3.979916532165268*^9, 3.9799165333270397`*^9}, {
  3.9799211754134636`*^9, 3.979921274573759*^9}, {3.979929006647356*^9, 
  3.9799291355415*^9}, {3.9799291759456444`*^9, 3.979929176025652*^9}, {
  3.979940054673992*^9, 3.979940073147093*^9}, {3.979947248031868*^9, 
  3.9799472751711006`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"59080e10-f1c9-be4c-97bf-\
10d25dec785b"],

